# =============================================================================
# HOMZEN REAL ESTATE DESIGN SYSTEM (Cursor Rules)
# =============================================================================
# Strict 1:1 clone of target Homzen landing page design.
# Apply these rules to ALL component creation and redesigns.

## TYPOGRAPHY HIERARCHY
- HEADINGS (H1, H2, H3, section titles, hero headline): 
  Font: 'Poppins' (sans-serif, NO SERIFS, font-sans)
  Weights: font-bold (700) or font-semibold (600)
  Color: `text-hz-ink` (light reference: #1A1A2E)
  Letter-spacing: -0.5px
  Line-height: 1.15 to 1.2 (tight, clean)
  
- BODY TEXT (descriptions, property features, paragraph text):
  Font: 'Poppins' (sans-serif)
  Weights: font-regular (400) or font-medium (500)
  Color: `text-hz-body` (light reference: #555555)
  Line-height: 1.6 to 1.65 (breathing room)

- UI TEXT (buttons, labels, tags, filters, prices, counts):
  Font: 'Poppins' (sans-serif)
  Weights: font-medium (500) or font-semibold (600)
  Color: Varies by context (see COLOR TOKENS below)
  Font-size: 12px to 16px (crisp, precise)

- SMALL TEXT (metadata, captions, helper text):
  Font: 'Poppins' (sans-serif)
  Weight: font-regular (400)
  Color: `text-hz-muted` (light reference: #717171)
  Size: 11px to 13px

## COLOR TOKENS (REQUIRED — use these, not raw hex in components)
Runtime source of truth: `src/index.css` CSS variables → Tailwind `hz-*` classes.

Surfaces:
  - `bg-hz-page` — page canvas
  - `bg-hz-elevated` — cards / elevated panels
  - `bg-hz-sunken` — recessed / alternate sections
  - `bg-hz-footer` + `text-hz-footer-fg` — always-dark band (#1D2A3A); use for footer / dark CTA headers (never flips in navy theme)
  - Decorative depth: reuse `SectionAtmosphere` with real `image` props (`architecture` | `interior-dark` | `soft-left` | `aerial` | `interior-light`) from `public/bg/` — not gradients alone

Text / chrome:
  - `text-hz-ink` / `text-hz-dark` — headings, strong UI text
  - `text-hz-body` — body copy
  - `text-hz-muted` — metadata, captions
  - `border-hz-border` / `border-hz-line` — dividers

Accent / CTA (NEVER theme-shifted):
  - `bg-hz-primary` / `text-hz-primary` / `hover:bg-hz-primary-hover`
  - Soft orange locked: oklch(0.64 0.19 45) / hover oklch(0.56 0.20 42) (~#E07030 / ~#C85E22)
  - ONLY for primary CTAs, selected/active states, highlight text
  - Do NOT replace brand orange with blue just because navy theme is active

Light theme reference values (default `data-theme="light"`):
  - Page/elevated ≈ warm off-white / white; sunken ≈ #F5F5F5
  - Ink #1A1A2E, body #555555, muted #717171, line #E5E5E5

## DUAL THEME (light | navy)
- Mechanism: `html[data-theme="light|navy"]` remaps `--hz-*` (and luxury/paper/shadcn aliases). Components keep the same `hz-*` classes.
- Default: **light** (Homzen baseline). Navy is opt-in via header toggle; persisted in `localStorage` key `hz-theme`.
- Navy mental model: dark blue surfaces; light ink / body / muted / borders. Brand coral stays identical.
- Do NOT sprinkle Tailwind `dark:` variants across components for theming.
- Do NOT follow `prefers-color-scheme` automatically — this is a brand theme, not OS dark mode.
- Third-party: Turnstile + Leaflet tiles + Sonner must follow `useTheme()` when theme-aware.
- When adding colors, always use semantic tokens so both themes work.

## ICONOGRAPHY RULES (CRITICAL)
Property Feature Icons (Beds, Baths, Sq Ft, Garage, Type, Location):
  - STYLE: Bold, heavy-weight, detailed, intricate icons (NOT thin lines)
  - SOURCE: Font Awesome 6 (solid weight), Phosphor Icons (fill weight), or custom SVG
  - Weight: Bold/Solid appearance, fill-based (not stroke-based)
  - Size: 18px to 28px (prominent, not delicate)
  - Color: `text-hz-body` or `text-hz-ink` (theme-aware)
  - AVOID: Lucide React thin icons, stroke-based outlines (creates AI-slop look)

System / Utility Icons (Arrows, Chevrons, Close, Hamburger, Search, Filter, Theme toggle):
  - Use Lucide React for these functional utilities ONLY
  - Stroke weight: stroke-[1.5] or stroke-[2]
  - Color: `text-hz-body` or `text-hz-ink`
  - Size: 16px to 20px

Icon + Text Spacing:
  - gap-2 (8px) for compact UI elements
  - gap-3 (12px) for featured sections

## LAYOUT & WHITESPACE
Section Padding (Vertical):
  - py-20 (80px) for major sections
  - py-16 (64px) for moderate sections
  - py-12 (48px) for smaller sections
  - ALWAYS maintain breathing room

Container Max-Width:
  - max-w-7xl (1280px) for primary content
  - Horizontal padding: px-20 (80px) on desktop, px-10 (40px) on tablet, px-5 (20px) on mobile

Card Styling:
  - `bg-hz-elevated` with `shadow-hz-sm` / `shadow-hz-md`
  - Border-radius: rounded-xl (12px) or rounded-2xl (16px) or `rounded-hz`
  - Padding: p-6 (24px) for standard cards
  - Border: Optional `border-hz-border` (1px) for definition

Grid Layout (Property Cards, Feature Grid):
  - Desktop (1024px+): grid-cols-4 for standard cards
  - Tablet (768px+): grid-cols-2
  - Mobile (< 768px): grid-cols-1
  - Gap: gap-6 (24px) between cards

Hover States:
  - Subtle lift: hover:shadow-lg
  - Smooth transition: transition-all duration-300
  - Text color shift: hover:text-hz-primary
  - Keep refined, no aggressive transforms

## BUTTON STANDARDS
Primary Button (CTA):
  - `bg-hz-primary`, text-white
  - px-6 py-3 (24px × 12px)
  - font-poppins font-semibold text-sm
  - rounded-lg / rounded-hz, shadow-sm
  - hover:bg-hz-primary-hover, transition-colors duration-200

Secondary Button:
  - `bg-hz-sunken`, `text-hz-ink`
  - px-6 py-3
  - font-poppins font-medium text-sm
  - rounded-lg
  - hover: opacity/border via theme tokens

Outline Button:
  - border border-hz-border, bg-transparent, `text-hz-ink`
  - px-6 py-3
  - font-poppins font-medium text-sm
  - rounded-lg
  - hover:border-hz-primary, hover:text-hz-primary

## RESPONSIVE DESIGN
- Mobile-First: Design for 375px, scale up
- Breakpoints: sm (640px), md (768px), lg (1024px), xl (1280px)
- Hero Section: Single column on mobile, side-by-side on desktop
- Property Grid: Adjust columns per breakpoint
- Typography: Reduce heading size on mobile (text-4xl → text-2xl)
- Padding: Reduce px on mobile; increase on desktop

## COMPONENT ARCHITECTURE
- Use Tailwind Utility Classes exclusively
- Leverage component reusability (Card, Button, Badge, IconLabel)
- Map colors through `hz-*` tokens (no arbitrary hex in components)
- Use Next.js Image component for all property photos when applicable; otherwise optimized img
- Implement lazy-loading for below-fold images

## STRICT DO's AND DON'Ts
DO:
  ✓ Use 'Poppins' for ALL text (serif-free)
  ✓ Use bold/solid icons for property features (Font Awesome/Phosphor solid)
  ✓ Apply `bg-hz-page` / `bg-hz-elevated` / `bg-hz-sunken` for sections
  ✓ Use `text-hz-primary` / `bg-hz-primary` ONLY for primary CTAs and highlights
  ✓ Keep soft orange brand color locked across light and navy themes
  ✓ Maintain generous section padding (py-20/py-16)
  ✓ Soft shadows (`shadow-hz-sm`) and rounded corners
  ✓ Test hover states on all interactive elements
  ✓ Keep icons bold, detailed, heavy-weight
  ✓ Verify both themes when changing colors

DON'T:
  ✗ Use serif fonts (no Cormorant Garamond, no Georgia)
  ✗ Use pure black (#000000); use `text-hz-ink`
  ✗ Over-use coral; reserve for primary emphasis
  ✗ Shift brand orange to blue in navy theme
  ✗ Theme via mass `dark:` class edits or CSS invert filters
  ✗ Use thin-stroke icons on property cards (Lucide only for utilities)
  ✗ Create cramped layouts; prioritize breathing room
  ✗ Use harsh shadows or aggressive transforms
  ✗ Mix serif and sans-serif on same component
  ✗ Hardcode hex colors in components; stick to `hz-*` tokens

## DESIGN REFERENCES
- Target Image: Homzen Landing Page (1:1 clone) — light theme baseline
- Primary Font: Poppins (NO serifs, all weights 400-700)
- Icon Style: Bold, solid, detailed, intricate (heavy-weight appearance)
- Primary Color: vibrant orange (oklch 0.64 0.19 45) for CTAs only — theme-locked
- Themes: light (default) + navy (opt-in blue dark surfaces)
- Tokens: `hz-page`, `hz-elevated`, `hz-sunken`, `hz-ink`, `hz-body`, `hz-muted`, `hz-line`, `hz-primary`